# Proposed .kiroignore — copy to the repo root as `.kiroignore`.
#
# The agent cannot write this file itself: Kiro's hardcoded permission scope
# denies agent writes to `.kiroignore`. That is deliberate, so an agent cannot
# remove its own read barrier. Install it manually.
#
# gitignore-style syntax. This is a READ barrier enforced across agent file
# tools, separate from .gitignore, which only controls what gets committed.
#
# Limitation worth knowing: .kiroignore governs the agent's file-reading tools.
# It does not sandbox shell commands, so an allowed `cat *` in permissions.yaml
# can still read these paths. Pair this with the shell deny rules in
# permissions.yaml.

# ---- Credentials ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
**/secrets/**
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# ---- Candidate PII ----
# The master resume holds full employment history, education, and contact
# details. Tailoring is driven by the rules in config/resume.yaml, so the agent
# never needs to read the resume body itself.
data/resume/**

# Generated artifacts embed the tailored resume and the resolved answers to
# application questionnaires, both full of personal data.
data/applications/**

# ---- Runtime data ----
# Holds discovered jobs, application state, and the candidate answer bank.
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal
